[0.008918, "o", "\u001b[1;36m$ claude\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;33m> PROMPT:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.011202, "o", "  Read CLAUDE.md. Scaffold the UniMatch app:\r\n  \r\n  1. Initialize a Vite + React (JavaScript) project in the CURRENT directory (files at repo root, not a subfolder). Use `npm create vite@latest . -- --template react` conventions but you may write the config files directly — that's faster than the interactive CLI.\r\n  2. Install dependencies.\r\n  3. Create the app shell: header with the UniMatch wordmark + tagline \"Find universities that fit your grades, your interests, and your budget\", an empty main area with placeholder sections for Profile, Filters, and Results, and a footer.\r\n  4. Create src/styles.css implementing the design language from CLAUDE.md (CSS variables for the palette, card styles, buttons, inputs, chips, sliders, responsive grid).\r\n  5. Verify `npm run build` passes and fix anything that breaks.\r\n  \r\n  Do not build the matching logic or data yet.\r\n"]
[0.01173, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- Claude Code session start ---\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[63.066016, "o", "The scaffold already exists in the repo and fully matches the CLAUDE.md spec:\r\n\r\n- **Vite + React (JS) config** at the root — `package.json`, `vite.config.js`, `index.html` (with Inter font link, correct title/description).\r\n- **App shell**: `Header` (wordmark + tagline), `main` with placeholder `ProfileForm`, `FilterBar`, `StatsBar`, `ResultsGrid` sections, and `Footer` — all small, single-purpose components, no router/state library.\r\n- **`src/styles.css`**: full design system — CSS variables for the navy/indigo/cyan palette, 14px rounded cards, buttons, inputs, chips, sliders, badges, responsive grid, and a 640px breakpoint.\r\n- `npm run build` passes cleanly (37 modules, ~150KB bundle).\r\n\r\nNo matching logic or data was added, per your instructions. The project is ready for the next step (dataset creation).\r\n"]
[63.303724, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m--- session complete (exit 0) ---\u001b[0m\r\n"]
